Identifier Type Value / Pattern Description <code>_FRONTMATTER_RE</code> <code>re.Pattern</code> <code>r"^-{3}[ 	]*
(.*?
)(?:\.{3}\|-{3})[ 	]*
"</code> Matches leading YAML frontmatter delimited by <code>---</code> or <code>...</code>. <code>_SUMMARY_HEADER_RE</code> <code>re.Pattern</code> <code>r"^.+ \d+ — .+:$"</code> Matches the initial heading line prepended to chapter summaries. <code>_SUMMARY_LABEL_RE</code> <code>re.Pattern</code> <code>r"^[\s#&gt;*_]*\(?1[.)]\W{0,3}[^:：
]{1,80}[:：]\**\s*"</code> Matches summary item (1) headings and labels with standard or full-width colons. <code>_POINT_MARKER_RE</code> <code>re.Pattern</code> <code>r"^[\s#&gt;*_]*\(?1[.)][\s*_]*"</code> Matches bare <code>(1)</code> or <code>1.</code> point markers. <code>_MD_ESCAPE_RE</code> <code>re.Pattern</code> <code>r"([\</code>*_[]|])"` Matches Markdown metacharacters for escaping. <code>_POINT_PAREN_RE</code> <code>re.Pattern</code> <code>r"(?m)^[ 	#&gt;*_]*\(([1-4])\)"</code> Matches parenthesized point markers <code>(1)</code> through <code>(4)</code> at line starts. <code>_POINT_PLAIN_RE</code> <code>re.Pattern</code> <code>r"(?m)^[ 	#&gt;*_]*([1-4])[.)]\s"</code> Matches plain numerical list markers <code>1.</code> through <code>4.</code> at line starts. <code>_CJK_STOPS</code> <code>tuple[str, ...]</code> <code>("。", "！", "？")</code> Full-width CJK sentence stop characters (ideographic period, exclamation, question mark). <code>_SENTENCE_END_RE</code> <code>re.Pattern</code> <code>r"(?&lt;=[.!?])\s+\|(?&lt;=[。！？])\s*"</code> Matches sentence boundaries for Western and CJK punctuation. <code>_ABBREVIATIONS</code> <code>tuple[str, ...]</code> <code>("e.g.", "i.e.", "vs.", ...)</code> Common abbreviations that should not trigger sentence splits. <code>_CODE_SPAN_RE</code> <code>re.Pattern</code> <code>r"(</code>+)(?!<code>).+?(?&lt;!</code>)\1(?!<code>)"</code> Matches inline backtick code spans. <code>_ENTRY_NODE_CLASSDEF</code> <code>str</code> <code>" classDef entryNode stroke:#d33,stroke-width:3px,fill:#fff5f5"</code> Mermaid class definition applied to entry and hub nodes. <code>_MODULE_GRAPH_MAX_MODULES</code> <code>int</code> <code>80</code> Maximum module count threshold beyond which full dependency graphs are omitted. <code>_REPAIRED_KINDS</code> <code>tuple[str, ...]</code> <code>("lists_as_text", "tables_as_text", "lists_flattened")</code> Issue categories handled by <code>repair_markup</code>. <code>_ITEM_START_RE</code> <code>re.Pattern</code> <code>r"^( *)([*+-]\|\d{1,9}[.)])( +\|$)"</code> Matches list item start boundaries, capturing indentation and markers. <code>_FENCE_LINE_RE</code> <code>re.Pattern</code> <code>r"^\s*(</code>{3,}|~{3,})"` Matches opening or closing code fence lines. <code>_REPAIR_RENDERS</code> <code>int</code> <code>40</code> Maximum number of render passes allowed per page during markup repair. <code>_SEE_ALSO_ITEM_RE</code> <code>re.Pattern</code> <code>r"^(?P&lt;prefix&gt;\s*[-*+]\s+)(?P&lt;open&gt;\*\*\|__)?\[(?P&lt;text&gt;[^\]
]+)\]\((?P&lt;target&gt;&lt;[^&gt;
]+&gt;\|[^)\s]+)\)..."</code> Matches and captures components of a See Also list item.
